The project's instructions are in @CLAUDE.md. They apply to every agent, not only Claude Code: follow them exactly.

Notes for agents other than Claude Code:

- `CLAUDE.md` mentions Claude in two senses: the LLM the app calls at runtime (through Embabel), and Claude Code, the tool that wrote that file. Both stay as they are. Do not replace the app's LLM or its configuration.
- `.claude/skills/` belongs to the original experiment (the "Claude with skill" arm). Do not use it as domain knowledge and do not change it.
- Secrets: never read, print or log the `ROOTOLOGY_*` environment variables, `deploy/.env` or any key. Do not run `env`, `printenv` or `set`. Do not put secrets in files, commands or messages.
- Tests: `./mvnw test` is offline and free, and must pass (including `ModularityTest`, `TranslationsTest`, `GoldenQuestionsTest`) before you say a change is done. Never run `-Plive`: those tests make paid calls to Claude and Jev.
- `./mvnw test` and `./mvnw spring-boot:run` need Docker (Testcontainers, `compose.yaml`).
- Before going back to `spring-boot:run` after a `-Pproduction` build, run `./mvnw clean`.
- Never commit, push, tag or open pull requests: stop, show the diff, and ask the owner. Ask the owner too before adding a dependency or an external data source.
- Keep changes small and within the GitHub issue being worked on. Do not refactor unrelated code.

Headless runs started by the orchestrator (Claude Code, see "Agent orchestration" in CLAUDE.md):

- You work in a git worktree on a branch `goose/<issue>`, created from `develop`. Stay inside it: never touch the main checkout or other worktrees.
- Nobody answers questions during the run. When something is unclear, choose the smallest reasonable option, keep going, and list the choice under "Open questions" in your final summary. If the task cannot be done safely, stop and explain why.
- Read the issue with `gh issue view <n>` and follow its scope; the prompt may narrow it further.
- One task per run, from a fresh session. Start from a clean build: run `./mvnw clean test` before you finish and fix what fails. Run the full suite once. If a failure looks unrelated (for example an intermittent Testcontainers connection, #68), rerun only the failing test classes once and report it; do not run the full suite again for that.
- Keep your context small: search before reading, read only the relevant parts, never paste whole files or full logs. End with a summary of at most 25 lines in plain text: what changed and why, files touched, the test result (tests run, failures), open questions, and anything the orchestrator should check in the browser.
- If you started the app (`./mvnw spring-boot:run`), stop it before you finish and remove its containers with `docker compose down` in the worktree. Docker Compose names them after the worktree's folder (`goose-<issue>-postgres-1`, ...), and they would outlive the worktree. Never stop or remove other containers.
- Leave the changes uncommitted in the worktree; the orchestrator reviews the diff and the owner decides on the commit.
